<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dương Đình Nghệ</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/937">937</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Duong Dinh Nghe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dương Đình Nghệ was a Vietnamese military leader who expelled the Southern Han forces from the Red River delta in 931 and governed it as an autonomous military governor of Tĩnh Hải circuit. He was murdered in 937 by his officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kieu-cong-tien">Kiều Công Tiễn</a>, whose call for Southern Han help was answered by Ngô Quyền, Dương's son-in-law, at Bạch Đằng in 938.</p></div>
